### Core concepts

```mdl
page types: Types and schema
  What a type is, how ECHO identifies it, and how it changes over time.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/types/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - A type is an Effect Schema with a typename and a version; its DXN `dxn:<typename>:<version>` is what each object stores
    - Object types and relation types: `Type.makeObject` and `Type.makeRelation`
    - Annotations such as label and icon, and what tools derive from them
    - Registering types with a database, and what fails without it
    - JSON Schema in and out
    - Types edited at runtime: `addFields` and `updateFields`
    - Versions and migrations: `Migration.define`, `defineRename` and `defineContent` [D-155]
    - Limits: peers on different versions of a type do not merge, and when migrations run outside a plugin is not documented yet
```
```mdl
page objects-relations: Objects and relations
  Typed records in one space, and the entities that join them.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/objects-relations/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Objects are typed records in one space; relations are entities that join a source and a target
    - The managed fields: id, type, meta keys and tags, label, deleted
    - A relation next to a reference field, shown with a WorksAt relation beside `Person.employer` [D-160]
    - Parents and children, and what removing a parent does
    - Removal marks an object deleted, and it stays in history until the next epoch
    - Snapshots versus live objects
    - Limits: the top level of an object is a record, and a relation needs both ends
```
```mdl
page references: References and DXNs
  How objects point at each other, and how a reference resolves.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/references/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - `Ref.Ref` stores the URI of its target
    - EIDs (`echo:///id`, `echo://space/id`) versus DXNs
    - `peek` versus `load` versus `Ref.loadAll`, and traversal in a query instead of loading
    - Limits: dangling references, removed targets, arrays that keep dangling entries, and `Ref.equals`
```
```mdl
page feeds: Feeds
  An append log of ECHO objects, as a tree of branches.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/feeds/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - A feed is an append log of ECHO objects, a tree of branches [FEEDS.mdl F-1.1, F-1.2]
    - Uses as examples, not kinds: AI chat, comments, messaging, event logs [F-3.1]
    - Rewrite by id, logical removal, and rewind as a branch [F-1.3, F-1.4, F-1.5]
    - Cursors, forward and backward walks, and fork points [F-5]
    - Indexing on or off, partial sync, and retention per branch [F-2, F-4.4]
    - When a feed fits better than objects
    - Links to Changes and branches for branches of objects
```
```mdl
page queries: Queries
  Filters, query shapes, traversal and live results.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/queries/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - `Filter` is the predicate and `Query` the shape around it
    - Traversal in both directions [echo-client QUERY.mdl F-7]
    - Order, windows and aggregates [F-8, F-9]
    - Sources through `Scope`: this space, the registry, a feed
    - Live results never finish; each source has only a pending state [F-3]. Never describe a query as complete
    - Local writes show in results before the write returns [F-2]
    - Limits: remote results are revalidated [F-5]
```
```mdl
page spaces: Spaces and databases
  The unit of sharing and replication, how it is stored, and the Hypergraph over all of them.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/spaces/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - A space is the unit of sharing and replication, with one database
    - Storage: SQLite in a worker, browser file storage or disk; a space is never loaded into memory whole [echo-sqlite F-3]; indexing, and queries compiled to SQL [F-4]; writes and flush [F-6]
    - Replication: each member holds a full copy, syncing over WebRTC or through EDGE
    - The Hypergraph: every reachable space as one graph, qualified EIDs, references across spaces and unreachable spaces, the in-process registry a query searches without `from()`, and `db` versus Hypergraph
    - Access in one paragraph: HALO controls members and roles, built on Keyhive, with a link [D-156]
```
```mdl
page changes: Changes and branches
  Every write as a change, how changes merge, history, and branches of objects.
  section: ECHO
  route: /docs/echo/concepts/changes/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Every write is a change on a CRDT document
    - Merge rules: the merge table, assignment versus Text edits, offline writes, and a subscriber that writes during a notification makes its own commit
    - History: `Obj.getChanges` with the device for each, `Obj.getVersion` at past heads, `Filter.changes`
    - Branches: `createBranch` from the tip or past heads, covering the object and what it references; `switchBranch` per device, cascading to children; `mergeBranch`, `syncBranch`, `deleteBranch`; `db.branch` for a separate live copy shown side by side
    - Feed branches stay on Feeds, linked
    - Limits: ECHO does not know what a field means, rules across objects are not enforced, schema versions do not merge, and a switch does not follow you to other devices
```

