## EDGE

EDGE is the set of services DXOS runs on Cloudflare Workers: an always-online peer for every space and identity. The
section explains EDGE's architecture and how ECHO, HALO, MESH and PLEX use it; it has only Start here, Core concepts and
Resources [D-232]. EDGE can read a space only when the space gives it more than `pull` access; HALO's Spaces and
membership says so, and EDGE has no page of its own on it [D-245]. DXOS operates EDGE; the pages cover no self-hosting and never link its source [D-237].
Swarms, signaling and ICE/TURN are MESH's; Connecting covers only the link between a device and EDGE [D-234].

### Start here

```mdl
page edge-overview: Overview
  What EDGE is, and where ECHO, HALO, MESH and PLEX use it.
  section: EDGE
  route: /docs/edge/overview/
  group: Start here
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - EDGE is an always-online peer for local-first apps, run by DXOS on Cloudflare Workers, with a Durable Object per identity and per space [D-280]
    - One diagram of devices, EDGE and peers, and what goes over each link: each device's WebSocket ends at the Router, which reaches the DB, compute and identity services [D-285]
    - A table of where ECHO, HALO, MESH and PLEX use EDGE, each linking its concept page
    - DXOS runs EDGE, and an app points at it with `runtime.services.edge.url`
```
```mdl
page why-edge: Why EDGE?
  Why a local-first system runs servers at all.
  section: EDGE
  route: /docs/edge/why-edge/
  group: Start here
  template: narrative
  status: spike
  covers:
    - The pattern: a space that syncs between two devices that are never online at the same time
    - Comparison: an app server that owns the data, against an always-online peer that holds a copy
    - Practical problems: devices rarely online together, queries over objects this device has not loaded, recovery when every device is lost, work that runs while you are offline
    - One line that EDGE reads a space only with more than `pull` access, linking HALO's Spaces and membership [D-245]
```

### Core concepts

```mdl
