## TILE

TILE is DXOS's design system: themed UI components and the tokens behind them [D-246]. Its core is `@dxos/react-ui`,
and `@dxos/ui-theme` is documented as part of its setup, since nothing renders styled without it [D-238]. The other
`react-ui-*` packages get one line each in a catalog, and four of them get a guide [D-240]. The learning path builds a
contacts screen with plain React state and connects it to ECHO only on its last page [D-239]. Live previews on these
pages are islands rendered in the page, never iframes [D-241]. It has six concept pages and eleven API family
pages [D-242]. The routes are under `/docs/tile/`.

### Start here

```mdl
page tile-overview: Overview
  What TILE is, the core and component packages, and where to start.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/overview/
  group: Start here
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - What TILE is in one paragraph: `@dxos/react-ui` and the `@dxos/ui-theme` tokens and build plugin it needs
    - A grid of live component demos that follows the page's light or dark theme; each card names its package and opens that package's guide [D-289]
    - The split between the core and the component packages, with a link to the catalog
    - Where to go next: Why TILE?, Build with a coding agent, then the learning path
```
```mdl
page why-tile: Why TILE?
  Why UI written by many hands still looks and behaves like one app.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/why-tile/
  group: Start here
  template: narrative
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Opening: an app whose screens are written by many people, with Composer's plugins as the example [D-280]
    - Themed primitives and semantic tokens, so a plugin never picks a raw color and every plugin follows light and dark
    - Composite components built on zag machines, so focus, keyboard and ARIA roles come with the component
    - One size scale, so a toolbar, a menu and a dialog line up without per-component padding
    - What TILE does not need: no ECHO and no PLEX, so it works in any React app
```
```mdl
page tile-build-with-agent: Build with a coding agent
  Point Claude Code, Codex or Cursor at the skills DXOS uses to build with TILE.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/build-with-a-coding-agent/
  group: Start here
  template: tutorial
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Links to the `composer-ui` and `composite-components` skills, and where each agent loads skills from [D-248]
    - No prompt builder for now [D-248]
    - The `/tile/llms-full.txt` file for an agent that reads docs
```

