### Core concepts

```mdl
page tile-theme-tokens: Theme and tokens
  Semantic tokens, cascade layers, and `classNames` instead of `className`.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/concepts/theme-and-tokens/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Semantic color tokens and the utilities each yields (`bg-*`, `text-*`, `border-*`); dark mode through `light-dark()`
    - The `--dx-*` variables components read, and the cascade layers that order the theme against an app's own styles
    - The `classNames` prop for overrides, and why a guessed token renders wrong
    - Classes are generated at build time, so the Vite plugin must see every source that uses one
```
```mdl
page tile-composite: Composite components
  `Foo.Root`, `Foo.Trigger`, `Foo.Content`: one namespace per component, one part per element.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/concepts/composite-components/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - Components export as namespaces from subpaths, such as `@dxos/react-ui/Dialog`
    - Parts, `asChild` and slots
    - Behavior and ARIA roles come from zag machines; components add no roles of their own
```
```mdl
page tile-layout-concept: Layout
  The Panel and ScrollArea container model, and the layout primitives.
  section: TILE
  route: /docs/tile/concepts/layout/
  group: Core concepts
  template: concept
  status: spike
  covers:
    - `Panel` rows (header, body, footer) and the height chain that lets a body scroll
    - `Flex`, `Grid` and `Container` instead of hand-written flex and grid classes; `gap` takes ramp steps
    - Sizing is physical (`w-*`, `h-*`); direction-sensitive spacing is logical (`ps-*`, `ms-*`)
```
```mdl
