          reader's text; the three open buttons look alike, each in the palette color nearest its agent's brand; the
          prompt is prefilled in the agent, not sent
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Relationship to dxos.org

  req F-7.1:
    when: a reader is on any dxos.org docs page
    then: the header shows the DXOS logo, linking home, and the dxos.org nav (Home, ECHO, Composer,
          Plugins, Blog, Docs); the footer links the same pages, every docs section in the
          topic switcher's order (ECHO, HALO, MESH, EDGE, SAGE, PLEX, TILE), GitHub and Discord [D-250],
          [D-274]

  req F-7.2:
    when: a reader looks for ECHO material on dxos.org
    then: every ECHO page is a page of this site map; no other ECHO guide remains

  req F-7.3:
    when: a dxos.org Webflow page renders
    then: its nav and footer link `/echo`, and the home page's ECHO card links `/echo`

  req F-7.4:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: it has the dxos.org Webflow nav and footer, with no docs header, search or sidebar, and its
          actions lead into `/docs/echo`; the Webflow styles sit in a cascade layer above the theme's global
          reset and below its base, component and utility layers, and stop at each embedded component, so the
          page keeps its typography and code samples and embedded components keep their styling

  req F-7.5:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: it shows live demos in one frame with a tab each, in order: a collaborative editor with a Mermaid diagram in its document, a table
          and board over one data set, a graph explorer, and an infinite canvas of nested drawings; they share two peers, Alice and Bob, and one space in the page;
          each shows one or both peers, and has a switch per peer that takes it offline

  req F-7.6:
    when: a reader opens `/echo`
    then: the demos start as the page loads, and each shows its content as soon as that content is in the space,
          without waiting for the other demos

  req F-7.7:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: the demos and the architecture diagram are dark, like the page, whatever theme the reader's system
          prefers

  req F-7.8:
    when: a reader reaches a demo on `/echo` before it has loaded
    then: the demo's place shows a placeholder of the demo's size that says it is loading, so the page does not
          shift when the demo arrives

  req F-7.9:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: each demo has a card with its title and a sentence or two about the data it shows and what to try
          in it

  req F-7.10:
    when: a reader is on the PLEX Overview
    then: it shows the four demos from `/echo` under What you can build, each with a narrative about the
          plugins that render it: which plugins load, what each contributes, and how they share the objects
          without importing each other; each demo runs on its own page in an iframe, so its styles stay off
          the docs page

  req F-7.11:
    when: a reader comes back to a page with demos after its tab has been in the background
    then: every demo still shows its peers and their content, as it did before the tab was hidden

  req F-7.12:
    when: a reader opens `/echo`
    then: every demo shows its content on every peer no later than the shared-runtime demos did (a median of
          7.8 s on a local production build), measured over the whole page rather than per demo
```

