```mdl
decision D-61: The demos share two peers, Alice and Bob, each one in-memory client under every demo's plugin app, and one space that holds every demo's content. Alice creates the space and Bob joins it by invitation while Alice seeds it: first the content several demos show, then each demo's partial, with the diagram, the largest, last. A demo shows its objects as soon as they are written. A peer's online switch applies to that peer in every demo. A demo names the object each peer opens, a peer can switch between a demo's objects, and the page lists its demos by id, in order. Fills in [D-58].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-54
  affects: [F-7.5, F-7.6]
  why: A runtime per demo started eight clients and twenty spaces and ran four invitations; on a production build the demos were ready about 5.1 s after navigation, 3.7 s of it after the script loaded. Bob also waited for the seed's final flush, 1.5 s, before his invitation started.
  rejected:
    - One space per demo on the shared clients: an invitation per demo, where one is enough.
```

