```mdl
decision D-208: Bookmarks saves links. A bookmark has `title`, `url` and `note`; `visits` and Record visit go away. The operation is Save link: it takes `{ url, title?, note? }`, adds a bookmark to the current space through `Database.Service`, files it with `DefaultParent.add`, and returns its URI, the way Composer's markdown Create operation does. Its App Graph action sits on the space's Bookmarks section and saves the address on the clipboard. The article edits the title and note and no longer runs an operation. The skill tells the assistant to save a link the user wants to keep, with a short title and their note. The inspector's operation form shows an input for an optional text field and leaves an empty field out of the input.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-operations, plex-guide-testing, app-framework-publishing]
  why: A bookmark whose only operation counted visits was a counter, not something a person would use. Saving a link with a note is what a bookmark is for, and it gives the assistant a natural reason to run the operation.
```

```mdl
decision D-209: The four live demos also appear on the PLEX Overview, under What you can build. Each demo, there and on `/echo`, has a narrative beside it. On `/echo` the narrative is about the data: the objects in the space and what ECHO does as peers edit, go offline and reconnect. On the PLEX Overview it is about the plugins: which plugins render the demo, what each contributes, and how they meet over the same objects. Both narratives sit in one file beside the demos, so the two pages describe the same demos. On the PLEX Overview each demo runs in its own iframe, with its own two peers and space, like the other embeds on docs pages.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-welcome, F-7.9, F-7.10]
  why: The demos show what you can build with PLEX as well as what ECHO does, and a reader needs to be told what they are looking at.
  rejected:
    - The `/echo` React islands placed directly on the Overview: docs pages keep app CSS in iframes, so the islands' theme styles would reach the Starlight page.
```

```mdl
decision D-210: The Bookmarks operation is Mark as read, which makes Bookmarks a reading list. A bookmark has `title`, `url`, `note` and `read`. Mark as read takes `{ bookmark }`, a reference to a bookmark, resolves it with `Database.resolve` and sets `read`; it has no output. Its App Graph action is on each bookmark's toolbar, through `createTypeExtension`. The article edits the title, the address and the note, and says whether the bookmark has been read. The skill tells the assistant to mark a bookmark as read when the user says they have read it. Bookmarks are created only through the + menu. The inspector passes a reference to the sample for a reference input, shows the sample after an operation with no output, and its sample picker follows the sample's label as it is edited. Supersedes the Save link parts of [D-208].
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-208
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-operations, plex-guide-testing, app-framework-publishing]
  why: Save link did what the + menu's create-object already does. Marking a bookmark as read changes an object that exists, which the path did not show, and gives the assistant a reason to run the operation.
```

```mdl
