```mdl
decision D-293: A card's header is one compact line: the demo's title, its package and an arrow to the guide. The grid is in twelfths so every card has room for that line: Kanban, Calendar, Markdown editor and Diagram take half the width and two rows; the spreadsheet two thirds of a row beside the force graph; the gallery half the width and two rows, with the map and chart stacked beside it. The calendar is the week view; the markdown editor pads its text off the card's edges; the spreadsheet keeps wheel and trackpad scrolling inside the grid, so the page neither scrolls nor swipes back or forward; the chart has one series and no legend; the globe flies a looping trip between its points along the lines that join them. The masonry card is titled Gallery. Amends [D-289].
