```mdl
decision D-294: TILE's API section has one page per component namespace, as `@dxos/react-ui`'s pages do, grouped by package. The core pages sit directly under API; each other package is a group nested after them, alphabetically and labelled without its `react-ui-` prefix (Calendar's group is `calendar`), with its pages in alphabetical order, at `/docs/tile/api/<package>/<namespace>/`. A page's `package` field places it. In every section a top-level group starts expanded and a nested group starts collapsed, opening when the current page is in it. Each namespace page opens with one of the package's own stories, embedded with `StoryEmbed` and with debug args turned off, then the import, the install, the parts and their props, and the examples that were the package guides. The package guides and the Component packages page are retired; Guides keeps the three that span packages. The Overview grid's cards open the namespace pages. Amends [D-238], [D-251] and [D-289].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [tile-overview, F-21.2, tile-api-reference]
  why: A reader looks for a component by the package they install and the namespace they import, and a package's stories already show it running, so the docs need no second copy of each demo.
  rejected:
    - One Overview page per package: the reader wants a page per component namespace, as for `@dxos/react-ui`.
    - A catalog page of every package: a package worth documenting gets its own group in API instead.
```

```mdl
decision D-295: Each card in the TILE Overview's grid runs a story from its package's own stories file, the same story that opens the card's API page. Kanban runs Board's `Default`, Calendar runs `Week`, and Markdown editor runs `WithToolbar`. Where no story fits a card, the package gains a `Docs` story with the demo the guide had: the spreadsheet, the force graph, the diagram, the gallery, the globe's trip and the chart. A `Docs` story fills its frame on the page's surface, whatever its meta's layout. The examples on those API pages keep their code, and the story at the top runs it. A story can change for the docs, as the editor stories pad their text, but a package's API does not. Amends [D-289], [D-293] and [D-294].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-21, tile-overview, tile-api-diagram-diagram, tile-api-geo-globe, tile-api-graph-graph, tile-api-grid-grid, tile-api-masonry-masonry, tile-api-plot-plot]
  why: A demo written for the docs alone is a second copy that drifts from the package; a story is checked in Storybook and runs the same in the grid, on the API page and in Storybook.
  rejected:
    - Snippets for the cards, as before: each card's demo lived only in the docs.
    - Existing stories for every card: the force graph's story is sized for a whole screen, and the others have no story for what the card shows.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext template
  uri: org.dxos.docs.template@1.0
  desc: A page format, as the ordered parts every page of that template has.
  fields:
    purpose: Prose
    parts: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext page
  uri: org.dxos.docs.page@1.0
  desc: One page of the docs. The inline prose is its summary; the block's position sets its sidebar order.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    section: Prose
    route: URI
    group: Prose
    template: ExtRef
    status: planned | spike | done | later
    covers?: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
